/* 
 By default → position: static;
   - Matlab element normal document flow me hota hai.
   - Top/left/right/bottom values ispe apply nahi hoti.
*/

/* 
 position: relative;
   - Is element ki apni jagah same rehti hai, 
     but tum top/left/right/bottom values use karke 
     element ko uski original jagah se shift kar sakte ho.
   - Baaki elements apni jagah pe rehte hain.
   Example: top: -20px → element upar shift ho jaata hai.
*/

/* 
 position: absolute;
   - Ye element apne nearest positioned ancestor (jisme static ke alawa koi position ho) 
     ke relative place hota hai.
   - Agar koi ancestor positioned nahi hai, to ye <html> (viewport) ke relative ho jaata hai.
   - Isme tum top/left/right/bottom values use karte ho.
    Exception: Agar parent pe transform, filter, ya perspective apply hai,
     to wo bhi positioned ancestor maana jaata hai.
*/

/* 
 position: fixed;
   - Ye element viewport (screen) ke relative fix ho jaata hai. 
   - Scroll karne par bhi same jagah par rehta hai.
   Example: chat bubble / "scroll to top" button.
*/

/* 
 position: sticky;
   - Ye element normal flow me hota hai, 
     but jaise hi tum scroll karte ho aur uski defined top/bottom point aata hai,
     ye element wahin "stick" ho jaata hai.
   - Mostly navbar design me use hota hai.
*/

/* 
 z-index
   - Jab elements overlap hote hain, to z-index decide karta hai kaun upar hoga.
   - By default z-index: auto hota hai.
   - Agar tumhe ek box ko dusre box ke upar lana hai → z-index: 1 (ya koi bhi positive value).
   - Larger value = upar dikhai dega.
*/
